From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] audio: keep ALSA playback nonblocking during shutdown

SDL_CloseAudioDevice joins the playback thread after clearing enabled. A
blocking snd_pcm_writei can wait forever on the handheld's ALSA shared PCM
and never observe that flag. Use SDL's existing nonblocking playback path,
which waits for space and retries writes while checking enabled.

--- a/src/audio/alsa/SDL_alsa_audio.c
+++ b/src/audio/alsa/SDL_alsa_audio.c
@@ -25,3 +25,3 @@
 #ifndef SDL_ALSA_NON_BLOCKING
-#define SDL_ALSA_NON_BLOCKING 0
+#define SDL_ALSA_NON_BLOCKING 1
 #endif
